Welcome to M Plus Plus! 
The visual math coding language

To get started you can click file and then new to make a new mpp file
Or open an existing mpp file
You can save this file using save (ctrl+s)

To get started with math use := to assign variables

ex: a:=5+5
a is stored with a value of 10

you can then print using the print function
print(a)

printing also can function on its own
print(5+5)

Click run to display in the terminal!

You can try this out with real and complex numbers with standard mathmatical operations (+,-,*,/)
In all sorts of sets (\mathbb{R},\mathbb{Q},\mathbb{C},\mathbb{N})

Use \ to Start a new math query.
Press enter to confirm your selection

You can use this to visualize all sorts of math symbols such as \frac{}{},\exp{}{},\sqrt[]{}
These are all usable just how you would in Desmos or Symbolab
The symbols are standard latex and can be pasted from latex documents
And yes you can assign them to variables

We also provide matrix support
Start a matrix math query and you can do all sort of operations

ex: a:=\begin{bmatrix}1&1\\2&2\end{bmatrix}\times\begin{bmatrix}4&2\\2&3\end{bmatrix}
print(a)
(note the times symbol can just be the standard * from your keyboard 
but we also support the "times" symbol from query)

And just like that the result is printed!

Like any normal text editor we have standard editing commands 
they are tied to standard keybinds ctrl+c (copy),ctrl+v (paste), ctrl+z (undo)...


